CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20260915T183304Z
DESCRIPTION:This joyful St. Cecilia's Day celebration honors music's patro
 n saint with works by Purcell and Handel. From Purcell's sparkling "Welco
 me to All the Pleasures" to Handel's tributes to Cecilia\, this program e
 xplores the rich culture of celebration\, ceremony\, and artistic homage 
 in seventeenth- and eighteenth-century England.\n\nThe program for the co
 ncert is:\n* Alessandro Scarlatti: Cantantibus Organis\n* Handel: Look do
 wn\, Harmonious Saint\n* Handel: Cecilia\, volgi un sguardo\n* Purcell: L
 audate Ceciliam\n* Purcell: If Music Be the Food of Love\n* Purcell: Welc
 ome to All the Pleasures\n\nFree admission. Paid parking is available at 
 the Bryan Center Parking Garage at 125 Science Dr. with ADA parking in th
 e surface lot at the same address.\n\nLearn more about the composition an
 d history of the music in a pre-concert talk by musicology graduate stude
 nt Tavish Daly at 4:00 p.m. in the Divinity School's Goodson Chapel.\n\nF
 amilies with young children and those who are not able to attend the conc
 ert are invited to come to an open rehearsal the day before the concert\,
  November 21\, between 1:30 and 4:00 p.m. in Duke Chapel.\n\nBach's canta
 tas stand among the great achievements of sacred music\, uniting theologi
 cal depth\, dramatic immediacy\, and extraordinary musical invention. The
  2026-2027 series\, "Odes & Oratorios\," explores music ranging from inti
 mate devotion to public celebration\, from chamber-scale reflection to wo
 rks of festive grandeur.
DURATION:PT1H30M
