CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20261029T171604Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join AGS for an Evening with Brett McGurk on Monday\, N
 ovember 23rd.  \n\nBrett McGurk is a diplomat\, presidential advisor\, CN
 N Global Affairs Analyst\, and author. He has served in four presidential
  administrations across both parties and has been deeply involved in Midd
 le East military strategy\, diplomacy\, and U.S. policy for more than two
  decades. He has served directly for the last four presidents\, negotiate
 d multiple hostage releases\, built the international coalition that ulti
 mately defeated ISIS\, and engaged regularly and directly with leaders fr
 om across the Middle East and around the world.   \n\n \n\nMr. McGurk off
 ers insight into complex world problems\, and how he built successful coa
 litions\, advised four very different presidents\, and acted as a steady 
 and reliable leader to resolve seemingly insurmountable conflicts-earning
  strong bipartisan support in our divisive times. He shares his perspecti
 ve on the current state of world affairs\, the personalities who shape to
 day's headlines and their impact on industries such as energy\, global fi
 nancial markets\, and the U.S. economy. \n\nHis latest book\, Brink: Insi
 de the Race to Free the October 7th Hostages is the first insider account
  of the high-stakes multilateral negotiations to free the hostages taken 
 by Hamas during the October 7\, 2023\, attacks. A limited number of copie
 s of Brink will be available for free for attendees on a first-come\, fir
 st-serve basis. \n\nWe are excited for Mr. McGurk to discuss his career\,
  experience\, and book with our students and community members.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20261110T172550Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261123T173000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110T172550Z
